//shakirraza.onrender.com/static/cv.pdf"}},W5=[{id:"full-stack",number:"01",title:"Full-stack development",tagline:"Flask backends, clean frontends, auth & deploy-ready structure",description:"Small to mid products from UI to database with session-based admin tools and file storage.",points:["Flask + Jinja + Tailwind / Modern UI","Supabase / Postgres, sessions & secure CRUD","Admin CMS, file uploads, env-based config","Landing pages and portfolio-style sites"]},{id:"ai-ml-pipelines",number:"02",title:"AI & ML pipelines",tagline:"Preprocessing, baselines, model comparison & honest evaluation",description:"From raw data to a model you can defend: cross-validation, clean pipelines, and metrics that hold up under review.",points:["EDA, cleaning, feature prep (Pandas, NumPy)","Scikit-learn, XGBoost, LightGBM, Ridge & more","Cross-validation and honest evaluation (RMSLE, ROC-AUC)","Notebook → script → simple API handoff"]},{id:"data-scraping",number:"03",title:"Data scraping & ingestion",tagline:"Structured scraping, deduping & automated ETL loads",description:"Pull data from APIs or the web, clean it, and store it in a shape you can actually use for analytics or ML.",points:["Public APIs (e.g. job boards, open data, Adzuna)","Structured scraping where allowed & respectful","Deduping, normalization, scheduled-friendly scripts","Load into Supabase / PostgreSQL / CSV"]},{id:"backend-apis",number:"04",title:"Backend & REST APIs",tagline:"Endpoints, validation, rate limits & storage integration",description:"Reliable Python services: auth-aware routes, image handling, rate limiting, and seamless database wiring.",points:["REST APIs with Flask & FastAPI","Auth-aware routes and admin tools","Image/PDF handling and optimization (Pillow)","Supabase storage & database wiring"]},{id:"dashboards-data-apps",number:"05",title:"Dashboards & data apps",tagline:"Interactive Plotly charts & web dashboards over live feeds",description:"Turn tables and live feeds into something people can explore — filters, charts, and a simple UI instead of raw spreadsheets.",points:["Plotly charts and interactive visual views","Web dashboards on top of cleaned data","Internal tools and exploratory filters for small teams","Real-time data feeds with responsive layouts"]},{id:"llm-features",number:"06",title:"LLM features & assistants",tagline:"Groq / Llama 3.1 integrations grounded in database context",description:"Assistants grounded in your content — project FAQs, docs, or database context — with limits so costs stay under control.",points:["Groq / OpenAI-style LLM chat integrations","Context grounding from DB, docs, or case studies","Rate limits, short answers, and safe fallbacks","Custom system prompts and function calling"]}],$5=[{id:"job-market-analytics-dashboard",number:"01",title:"Job Market Analytics Dashboard",subtitle:"End-to-End Ingestion, Database Pipeline & Salary Regression",category:"AI / ML & Data Science",description:"End-to-end pipeline that pulls live job postings, cleans and stores them in Supabase, and predicts salaries with a validated regression model — exposed through a dashboard, not only a notebook.",longDescription:"Built a Python pipeline against the Adzuna API: fetches live postings, normalizes titles and locations, deduplicates, and stores structured records in Supabase. Trained a Ridge regression model for salary prediction and compared it against stronger baselines with 5-fold cross-validation. Exposed the live data through an interactive dashboard UI.",architectureDetails:["Adzuna API ingestion with query rate limiting and pagination handling","Automated data cleaning, title normalization, and feature preparation with Pandas","Supabase (PostgreSQL) structured table storage with relational indexing","Ridge salary prediction model with cross-validated performance metrics","Interactive dashboard UI built with Flask and Plotly visualizations"],metrics:[{label:"Data Source",value:"Live Adzuna API"},{label:"Database",value:"Supabase Postgres"},{label:"Model",value:"Ridge Regression"}],technologies:["Python","Flask","Supabase","Pandas","Scikit-learn","Plotly","REST API"],image:"https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/job-market-analytics-dashboard-0.png",screenshots:["https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/job-market-analytics-dashboard-0.png","https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/job-market-analytics-dashboard-1.png","https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/job-market-analytics-dashboard-2.png"],demoUrl:"https://job-market-dashboard-ton7.onrender.com/",githubUrl:"https://github.com/Shakir-Raza/job-market-dashboard",featured:!0,caseStudy:{problem:"Job boards show titles and salary ranges, but not a clear estimate of what a role should pay given skills, location, and seniority. Manual research is slow and biased. I wanted a system that ingests live postings, cleans the noise, and estimates salary in a way I could measure — not a one-off spreadsheet.",approach:"Built a Python pipeline against the Adzuna API: fetch postings, normalize titles and locations, remove duplicates, and store structured records in Supabase. Trained a Ridge regression model for salary prediction and compared it against stronger baselines so the metric was honest. Exposed the data through a dashboard so results are usable, not stuck in a notebook.",architecture:"Adzuna API → cleaning / feature prep (Pandas) → Supabase (Postgres) → Ridge salary model → dashboard UI (Flask / Plotly). Config via environment variables; Git for versioning.",challenges:"Inconsistent job titles; missing or very wide salary bands; duplicate postings across queries; keeping the pipeline reproducible when API responses or rate limits change.",results:"Live path from Adzuna into Supabase with cleaned records. Dashboard for exploring postings and predictions instead of raw CSV dumps.",lessons:"Data cleaning and schema design took more time than the model — and mattered more. A simple, well-validated model beat jumping to complex ones without a clear baseline.",nextSteps:"Richer features (skills extracted from descriptions), scheduled data refreshes, and a small API endpoint so other tools can query salary predictions."}},{id:"portfolio",number:"02",title:"Full-Stack Portfolio with AI Assistant",subtitle:"Supabase CMS, Image Optimization & Groq LLM Assistant",category:"Full Stack & LLM Integration",description:"Full-stack portfolio with Supabase-backed projects, admin CMS, image optimization, dark/light theme, and a Groq LLM assistant that answers questions about my work.",longDescription:"A production application that serves as the product itself. Built with Flask, Supabase (Postgres + Storage), session-based admin authentication for project CRUD, Pillow-based image optimization on upload, and a rate-limited chat endpoint powered by Groq (Llama 3.1) grounded in real project context.",architectureDetails:["Flask backend routes with Jinja templates and session authentication","Supabase PostgreSQL database storing projects, tags, metrics, and case studies","Pillow image optimization pipeline on upload (resizing, format conversion)","Groq LLM endpoint (Llama 3.1) with project context injection and rate limits","SEO fundamentals including dynamic sitemap, robots.txt, and canonical tags"],metrics:[{label:"LLM Engine",value:"Groq Llama 3.1"},{label:"Storage",value:"Supabase Cloud"},{label:"Backend",value:"Python / Flask"}],technologies:["Python","Flask","Supabase","LLMs","Groq","Llama 3.1","PostgreSQL"],image:"https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/portfolio-4.png",screenshots:["https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/portfolio-4.png","https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/portfolio-5.png","https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/portfolio-6.png","https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/portfolio-7.png"],demoUrl:"https://shakirraza.onrender.com/",githubUrl:"https://github.com/Shakir-Raza/portfolio",featured:!0,caseStudy:{problem:"Static portfolio templates don’t show backend skill. I needed a site that is the product itself: dynamic projects from a database, an admin I control, case-study fields, and an assistant that can talk about real work — not hardcoded HTML.",approach:"Built a Flask app with Jinja templates, Supabase for project data and image storage, session-based admin auth for create/edit/delete, Pillow-based image optimization on upload, SEO basics (sitemap, robots, meta), and a rate-limited chat endpoint powered by Groq (Llama 3.1) with live project context from the database.",architecture:"Browser → Flask routes → Supabase (Postgres + Storage). Chat: user message + history + project summaries → Groq API → short reply. Admin session auth; public pages read-only. Optional contact form via SMTP.",challenges:"Keeping chatbot answers short and accurate; dependency conflicts in production; making the UI feel intentional without looking like a generic AI template; environment-specific URLs for sitemap and canonical tags; safe uploads (type checks, size limits, CSRF).",results:"Live portfolio with CMS, optimized uploads, dark/light theme, services and contact pages, and an assistant grounded in project fields (problem / approach / results). The site itself demonstrates full-stack and LLM integration end to end.",lessons:"Shipping the full loop (data → admin → public UI → assistant) taught more than isolated demos. Small product decisions — rate limits, image size, theme persistence, honest case studies — compound fast.",nextSteps:"Deeper case studies on every project, custom domain, light analytics on which case studies get read, and tighter LinkedIn/CV alignment with the same top three projects."}},{id:"house-prices-prediction",number:"03",title:"House Prices Prediction Pipeline",subtitle:"Comparative ML Pipeline: Ridge, XGBoost, LightGBM & Gradient Boosting",category:"Machine Learning & Predictive Modeling",description:"End-to-end ML pipeline comparing Ridge, XGBoost, LightGBM, and Gradient Boosting on housing data with the same preprocessing and 5-fold cross-validation.",longDescription:"Used the housing dataset (79 features, 1,460 samples). Performed thorough exploratory data analysis, handled missing values, high-cardinality categorical encoding, and trained Ridge, XGBoost, LightGBM, and Gradient Boosting under a rigorous 5-fold cross-validation protocol.",architectureDetails:["Exploratory Data Analysis and data cleansing across 79 raw features","Consistent preprocessing pipeline with skew transformation and target encoding","Comparative benchmarking across 4 model families (Ridge, XGBoost, LightGBM, GBDT)","5-fold cross-validation tracking Root Mean Squared Logarithmic Error (RMSLE)","Feature importance attribution and residual diagnostics"],metrics:[{label:"Best RMSLE",value:"0.112 (5-Fold CV)"},{label:"Features Evaluated",value:"79 Dimensions"},{label:"Models Compared",value:"4 Families"}],technologies:["Python","Scikit-learn","XGBoost","LightGBM","Pandas","NumPy"],image:"https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/house-prices-prediction-0.png",screenshots:["https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/house-prices-prediction-0.png","https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/house-prices-prediction-1.png","https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/house-prices-prediction-2.png","https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/house-prices-prediction-3.png","https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/house-prices-prediction-4.png","https://rdgbuqwghgktaaongwck.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/project-images/house-prices-prediction-5.png"],demoUrl:"https://github.com/Shakir-Raza/house-prices-prediction",githubUrl:"https://github.com/Shakir-Raza/house-prices-prediction",featured:!0,caseStudy:{problem:"House price prediction is a common tutorial topic, which makes it easy to overfit one model and call it done. I wanted a disciplined comparison: same features, same folds, clear metrics — so I could defend why one approach won.",approach:"Used the housing dataset (79 features, 1,460 samples). Ran EDA, handled missing values and categorical encoding, then trained Ridge, XGBoost, LightGBM, and Gradient Boosting under the same 5-fold cross-validation setup. Tracked RMSLE so scores were comparable and not inflated by a single lucky split.",architecture:"Raw CSV → EDA / preprocessing (Pandas, NumPy) → model training (Scikit-learn, XGBoost, LightGBM) → 5-fold CV metrics → comparison plots / report.",challenges:"Missing values and high-cardinality categoricals; keeping preprocessing identical across all models; resisting the urge to tune only the “cool” model without a linear baseline.",results:"Best configuration reached 0.112 RMSLE under 5-fold CV. Clear ranking across four model families with the same evaluation protocol. Documented which signals mattered most after preprocessing.",lessons:"Baselines first. Gradient boosting helped, but only after the data path was clean. Cross-validation stopped me from trusting one impressive score on a single split.",nextSteps:"Deeper feature-importance analysis, modest hyperparameter search with nested CV, and a thin Flask API to serve the chosen model."}},{id:"shoes-market",number:"04",title:"Shoes Market (E-Commerce Platform)",subtitle:"Full-Stack Footwear Marketplace & Inventory State Engine",category:"Full Stack & E-Commerce",description:"Full-stack e-commerce marketplace platform featuring catalog filtering across brands, real-time inventory management, cart state machine, and clean responsive UI.",longDescription:"An active full-stack commerce platform engineered with Python, Flask, and PostgreSQL. Features dynamic product filtering by brand (Jordan, Nike, Adidas, New Balance), size, price tiers, and category, backed by relational data models and admin inventory controls.",architectureDetails:["Relational PostgreSQL schema with product variants, sizing matrices, and inventory counts","Dynamic multi-facet filtering (Brand, Category, Size, Price Range)","Client-side cart state machine with session persistence","Responsive design engineered for mobile and desktop checkout flows"],metrics:[{label:"Catalog Engine",value:"Multi-brand Filter"},{label:"Database",value:"PostgreSQL"},{label:"Status",value:"In Active Development"}],technologies:["Python","Flask","PostgreSQL","TailwindCSS","JavaScript","REST API"],image:"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552346154-21d32810aba3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80",demoUrl:"https://mizaajsoles.onrender.com/",githubUrl:"https://github.com/Shakir-Raza",featured:!0,inProgress:!0,caseStudy:{problem:"Building a snappy e-commerce experience requires seamless filtering, accurate stock synchronization, and an intuitive product discovery interface without bloated frontend frameworks.",approach:"Developing a streamlined Flask architecture with PostgreSQL relational tables for products and inventory variants, paired with responsive Tailwind styling and client-side filtering.",architecture:"Client UI → Flask API routes → PostgreSQL database → dynamic product catalog and cart session management.",results:"Active development with live deployment handling product catalogs, brand filtering, and real-time inventory updates."}}],lo=[{id:"ai-ml",title:"AI, ML & Data Science",shortCode:"01 / ML",tagline:"Preprocessing, model comparison, cross-validation & evaluation",skills:[{name:"Python",level:"Core Language",description:"Primary language for ML modeling, data processing, and scripting.",highlight:!0},{name:"Scikit